getForm.description:
Returns the form's name, `kind`, `scene`, public URL (`url`), description, field definitions and settings. Each element of `fields` is a single-key object `{ "<api_code>": {...} }`, in field order.
Also answers for a table or a quick payment form token; `kind` says which it is.
The following are included when the matching parameter is `true`:
- `include_analytics`: each analysable field's definition carries `analytics`;
- `include_theme`: carries `theme` (the form theme);
- `include_field_rules`: carries `field_rules` (field display rules);
- `include_extended_attributes`: carries `extended_attributes` (source-tracking links);
- `include_transactions`: carries `transactions` (payment statistics) when the form is bound to a payment account.

createTable.description:
Creates a table. Same as creating a form, except:
- field types can only be the column types tables support: `TextArea`, `RadioButton`, `CheckBox`, `BooleanField`, `MobileField`, `NumberField`, `DateTimeField`, `EmailField`, `LinkField`, `AttachmentField`, `FormulaField`, `RelationField`;
- attachment columns do not accept limit properties such as count / size limits, and number / formula columns have limited precision; a violation returns 400 listing the offending columns;
- choice columns do not get an "Other" choice; `folder_token` must be a table folder; `layout` is not supported.
- with `with_default_entries: true`, 3 blank entries are added after creation (as when creating a table in the product); by default none are added.
Returns the table structure, including fields and views.
